      "subtitle": "The Piper of Dawn game is a single-player alchemy-shop-farming time-loop RPG developed by Bone Nail and co-published with 2P Games. It launched worldwide on Steam on September 22, 2026 under AppID 3804370, and Steam tags it Indie, RPG, Simulation, and Strategy with Shop Keeper, Farming Sim, Base Building, Story Rich, Multiple Endings, Lovecraftian, Choices Matter, and Singleplayer. The title is unrelated to Pink Floyd's 1967 album \"The Piper at the Gates of Dawn\".\n\n## Identity: developer, publisher, and Steam AppID\n\nThe Piper of Dawn game ships on Steam under AppID 3804370. Developer Bone Nail is listed as the primary studio on the Steam store page and on the Bone Nail publisher profile, with 2P Games appearing as a co-publisher. There is no separate edition or app ID for this project; the Steam store URL `store.steampowered.com/app/3804370/` resolves to the only canonical launch listing as of 2026-09-25.\n\nThe release date on the Steam store page is September 22, 2026. The store page is the authoritative source for developer, publisher, and release date, with SteamDB mirroring the same AppID and release data and the Bone Nail publisher profile confirming the studio name.\n\n### Why identity matters here\n\nTwo unrelated things show up when a player searches for this title: the 2026 Steam game and Pink Floyd's 1967 album \"The Piper at the Gates of Dawn\". Both phrases contain the words \"Piper\" and \"Dawn\", and search engines do not separate them. Confirming that the URL reads `store.steampowered.com/app/3804370/`, the developer is Bone Nail, and the tags include Singleplayer is the fastest way to be sure you have the right product.\n\n## Genre, tone, and Steam tags for The Piper of Dawn game\n\nThe Steam store page places The Piper of Dawn game in four genre pillars and a longer list of behaviour tags.\n\n- Genre pillars: Indie, RPG, Simulation, Strategy.\n- Behaviour tags: Shop Keeper, Farming Sim, Base Building, Story Rich, Multiple Endings, Lovecraftian, Choices Matter, Singleplayer.\n\nThe combination tells a player what to expect: a single-player, narrative-heavy RPG where you run a shop, build a base, and tend magical crops, with branching choices that drive different endings. The Lovecraftian tag sits alongside a Diamond City setting, which frames the tone as mythos-influenced rather than purely cozy.\n\nThe tags are read straight from the Steam store page for AppID 3804370. They do not include multiplayer, co-op, online play, or shared-screen variants, so single-player is the only confirmed mode at launch.\n\n## One-line pitch and gameplay identity\n\nThe single-line pitch is straightforward: an alchemy-shop-farming loop wrapped in a time-loop progression. You run a Diamond City shop, brew potions through the Tree of Life, plant and harvest magical crops, and grow your own Peoplesprouts workforce, then rewind the day through the Save and Load gods while Oracle blessings stack across loops.\n\nThe mechanics are unusual enough that the same loop plays differently on each run. Save and Load lets you carry upgrades forward, and Oracle blessings change the rules for the next loop, so a run that ends in failure still leaves the shop a little closer to a future ending. Multiple endings and six faction tracks branch the outcome, and the cast includes six central heroines and forty or more named NPCs.\n\n## Pink Floyd album disambiguation\n\nPink Floyd's 1967 album \"The Piper at the Gates of Dawn\" is the most common unrelated result that shares words with this game. The album is music, not a video game, and the title is the only thing in common. Steam does not list any Pink Floyd product under AppID 3804370, and the Bone Nail publisher profile does not mention the album.\n\nThree quick checks confirm you are looking at the game rather than the album.\n\n- The URL reads `store.steampowered.com/app/3804370/` for the game, not a music store or a Wikipedia entry for the album.\n- The developer is Bone Nail, with 2P Games listed as co-publisher, not a record label.\n- The tags include Indie, RPG, Simulation, Strategy, and Singleplayer, not music, vinyl, or remaster.\n\nAny page that lists Pink Floyd, a record label, or a 1967 release year is not the game. Pink Floyd's album is referenced here only so launch-day searchers do not bounce between the two products.\n\n## Where to read next\n\nThree pages answer the launch-day follow-up questions without overlapping the explanation on this page.\n\n- The [release status](/release) page confirms the September 22, 2026 launch date and the October 6, 2026 introductory discount end.\n- The [Steam availability](/steam) page confirms AppID 3804370, single-player status, the 91 Steam Achievements count, and the demo reference.\n- The [gameplay loop](/gameplay) page explains how the four pillars (alchemy, farming, shop, time loop) tie together for a new player.",
