        "body": "## Demo FAQ\n\n### When was The Piper of Dawn demo available?\n\nThe Piper of Dawn demo was available during Steam Next Fest in February 2026, hosted on the Steam store page for AppID 3804370. Whether the demo stays accessible after launch is not announced as of 2026-09-25.\n\n### What content did The Piper of Dawn demo include?\n\nThe Piper of Dawn demo included the prologue of Diamond City, early alchemy crafting with the Tree of Life and Equivalent Exchange rules, and the basics of shopkeeping. It did not include the full multi-ending branching or late-game faction reputation shifts.\n\n### Is The Piper of Dawn demo still playable after launch?\n\nNot announced as of 2026-09-25. Bone Nail and 2P Games have not stated whether the February 2026 demo remains downloadable after the September 22, 2026 release. Check the Steam store page directly for current demo status.\n\n### Can I use The Piper of Dawn demo progress in the full game?\n\nNot announced as of 2026-09-25. The Steam store page does not state whether demo saves carry over. Treat save transfer as a separate question from demo availability.\n\n### Will there be a new The Piper of Dawn demo after launch?\n\nNot announced as of 2026-09-25. There is no published Bone Nail or 2P Games roadmap for a post-launch demo. Any future demo or festival appearance should be treated as a new dated announcement.\n\n### How long was The Piper of Dawn demo?\n\nThe demo ran for the prologue of Diamond City, covering the opening time-loop introduction, the first alchemy tutorial, and the early shopkeeping loop. The slice is short enough to complete in a single sitting for most testers."
